Subject: [PATCH 28/61] NNS.ARMA.optim: actually evaluate the equal-weights
 candidate

For multi-period selections the optimizer meant to compare the
NNS.seas-based weights with equal weights, but weight.SSE was computed
from the weights = NULL forecast, so it always equalled nns.SSE,
'weight.SSE < nns.SSE' could never hold and $weights was always NULL.
Forecast with weights = rep(1/k, k) first, score that, and keep the
weights = NULL forecast when equal weights are not better.

Evidence: 50 + 5 sin(2 pi t/12) + 4 sin(2 pi t/7) + N(0, 1.5^2), n = 160,
h = 10, seasonal.factor = c(4,6,7,12,14,24), 25 seeds: 5 multi-period
selections; equal weights now chosen in 2 of them (before: never).
  seed 9  (lin, periods 12 7):  validation MSE NULL 9.719 vs equal 9.644
     weights NULL -> 0.5 0.5; results 51.683 51.226 50.361 -> 51.563 51.391 50.698
  seed 17 (both, periods 12 14): weights NULL -> 0.5 0.5,
     results 56.004 53.703 53.368 -> 55.574 53.990 54.298
Single-period selections, and multi-period ones where equal weights do
not improve the objective, are unchanged (all AirPassengers/VIX configs
identical).
---
 R/ARMA_optim.R | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/ARMA_optim.R b/R/ARMA_optim.R
index 0b8f7f8..64b4b0f 100644
--- a/R/ARMA_optim.R
+++ b/R/ARMA_optim.R
@@ -357,8 +357,15 @@ NNS.ARMA.optim <- function(variable,
     nns.SSE <- min(unlist(overall.estimates))
     predicted <- NNS.ARMA(variable, training.set = training.set, h = h_eval, seasonal.factor = nns.periods, method = nns.method, plot = FALSE, negative.values = negative.values, weights = NULL)
     
-    if(length(nns.periods)>1){
-       weight.SSE <- eval(obj.fn)
+    if(length(nns.periods) > 1){
+      # Candidate: equal weights across the selected periods. (weight.SSE used
+      # to be evaluated on the weights = NULL forecast, i.e. equal to nns.SSE,
+      # so equal weights could never be chosen.)
+      predicted.null <- predicted
+      predicted <- NNS.ARMA(variable, training.set = training.set, h = h_eval, seasonal.factor = nns.periods, method = nns.method, plot = FALSE, negative.values = negative.values, weights = rep(1/length(nns.periods), length(nns.periods)))
+      weight.SSE <- eval(obj.fn)
+      if(is.na(weight.SSE)) weight.SSE <- Inf
+      predicted <- predicted.null
       
       if(weight.SSE < nns.SSE){
         nns.weights <- rep((1/length(nns.periods)),length(nns.periods))
@@ -398,7 +405,14 @@ NNS.ARMA.optim <- function(variable,
     predicted <- NNS.ARMA(variable, training.set = training.set, h = h_eval, seasonal.factor = nns.periods, method = nns.method, plot = FALSE, negative.values = negative.values, weights = NULL)
     
     if(length(nns.periods) > 1){
+      # Candidate: equal weights across the selected periods. (weight.SSE used
+      # to be evaluated on the weights = NULL forecast, i.e. equal to nns.SSE,
+      # so equal weights could never be chosen.)
+      predicted.null <- predicted
+      predicted <- NNS.ARMA(variable, training.set = training.set, h = h_eval, seasonal.factor = nns.periods, method = nns.method, plot = FALSE, negative.values = negative.values, weights = rep(1/length(nns.periods), length(nns.periods)))
       weight.SSE <- eval(obj.fn)
+      if(is.na(weight.SSE)) weight.SSE <- -Inf
+      predicted <- predicted.null
       
       if(weight.SSE > nns.SSE){
         nns.weights <- rep((1/length(nns.periods)),length(nns.periods))
